From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:24:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Use the manual's PLL_AUDIO0 point for
 22.5792 MHz

The 22.5792 MHz x 4 entry of PLL_AUDIO0's sigma-delta table is the
A523's: N = 75, P0 = 20 and pattern 0xa002872b (triangular 1-bit mode,
32 kHz slope, bottom 0x0872b). The A733 manual gives its own point for
this rate in the PLL table: N = 67 plus the fraction 0x179a7 / 2^17
(VCO 1625.7024 MHz), divided by P0 = 18. Both produce 90.3168 MHz, but
only the second is documented for this SoC.

Use the documented point. The pattern follows the manual's fractional
division setting: SIG_DELT_PAT_EN (bit 31) set, SPR_FREQ_MODE = 3 as
recommended, WAVE_STEP = 0, so WAVE_BOT carries the fraction. Bit 31 is
part of the pattern because ccu_sdm compares the pattern against the
whole PAT0 register when it reads the rate back.

Not covered: the PAT1 enable bits (PLL_PI_EN, PLL_SDM_EN) stay as the
CCU driver sets them.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; during a 44.1 kHz OWA
stream PLL_AUDIO0 reads 0xF9114200 (N 67, P0 18, locked), PAT0
0xE00179A7 and PAT1 0xB8000000, and pll-audio0-4x runs at 90.3168 MHz.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index efcf5ff0def7..700cae872ece 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -353,10 +353,16 @@ static struct ccu_nkmp pll_ve1_clk = {
  * ignore the divider and force it to 1 (encoded as 0), in the probe function
  * below.
  * The M factor must be an even number to produce a 50% duty cycle output.
+ *
+ * The 22.5792 MHz x 4 point is the one in the A733 manual (Table 4-3):
+ * N = 67 plus the fraction 0x179a7 / 2^17, so the VCO runs at 1625.7024 MHz,
+ * divided by P0 = 18. The pattern is fractional division as described in
+ * the manual: SIG_DELT_PAT_EN set, SPR_FREQ_MODE = 3, WAVE_STEP = 0 and
+ * WAVE_BOT = 0x179a7.
  */
 #define SUN60I_A733_PLL_AUDIO0_REG	0x260
 static struct ccu_sdm_setting pll_audio0_sdm_table[] = {
-	{ .rate = 90316800, .pattern = 0xa002872b, .m = 20, .n = 75 }, /* 22.5792 * 4 */
+	{ .rate = 90316800, .pattern = 0xe00179a7, .m = 18, .n = 67 }, /* 22.5792 * 4 */
 };
 
 static struct ccu_nm pll_audio0_4x_clk = {
